course: dictionary
lesson: 7469
title: Pork and the French lords
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Pork» is a meat, and it comes from a pig. The clue is in the sentence: «A sausage at a barbecue is mostly minced pork.» Sausages are food you eat, so pork must be the meat inside them.
explain: Pork is a special kind of noun. You cannot count it, so you say some pork, not two porks or a pork. Try swapping your meaning into the sentence: «A sausage is mostly minced meat from a pig» still makes sense, so pork means meat from a pig.
explain: Look at the animal and the meat. The farmer looks after a pig, but on the lord's table the meat is called pork. English kept the animal names, but the meat names came from French, so pig is the animal and pork is the meat.
fact: Pork is meat that comes from a pig.
fact: Pork is uncountable: you say some pork, not two porks.
fact: Pork must be cooked all the way through to be safe to eat.
fact: Some people, for example many Jewish and Muslim people, do not eat pork for religious reasons.
fact: After 1066 English kept the animal words (pig) but took French meat words, so the meat became «porc», which is now pork.
exercise: «A sausage at a barbecue is mostly minced pork.» What is pork? | A small cow | *Meat that comes from a pig | A type of bread | A kind of vegetable
exercise: «Pork must be cooked all the way through to be safe.» Why must pork be cooked all the way through? | So it is cheaper | *So it is safe to eat | So it turns green | So it gets bigger
exercise: «The farmer keeps a pig, but the lord eats the pork.» Which word names the meat? | lord | pig | *pork | farmer
test: «Some people do not eat pork for religious reasons.» What does this tell you? | Pork is a kind of fish | Everyone eats pork at every meal | Pork is sold in every shop | *Some people choose not to eat pork because of their religion
test: «Pork comes from a farm animal.» Which animal does pork come from? | *A pig | A sheep | A cow | A chicken
exam: Ella asks, «How many porks are in the fridge?» Why is this question wrong? | Porks are pigs | There is no fridge | *Pork is uncountable, so we say some pork | Pork is always frozen
